<title>INDIA: India's IPCL 1996/97 net seen falling.</title>
<headline>India's IPCL 1996/97 net seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Indian Petrochemicals Corporation Ltd (IPCL) is likely to see its net profit falling 10.32 percent to 5.41 billion rupees in the year to March 31, 1997, a Reuter poll of 28 leading securities and brokerage firms said on Monday.</p>
<p>Projections ranged from 4.96 billion rupees to 6.40 billion</p>
<p>rupees against 6.04 billion in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>IPCL  ----PAT seen down 10.32%, sales off 1.64%</p>
<p>			Net profit  1995/96     Net sales  1995/96</p>
<p>				 (in million rupees)</p>
<p>Average		5,413.62   6,036.90   30,520.46   31,028.40</p>
<p>High		   6,401.00		  41,000.00</p>
<p>Low		    4,961.00		  27,331.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
